{"name":"Tennis Court","hex":"#c8450c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tennis court","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A firm, rectangular surface, marked with lines and having a net across the middle, where the game of tennis is played."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tennis_court"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tennis court","blocks":[{"text":"A tennis court is the venue where the sport of tennis is played. It is a firm rectangular surface with a low net stretched across the centre. The same surface can be used to play both doubles and singles matches. A variety of surfaces can be used to create a tennis court, each with its own characteristics which affect the playing style of the game."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Universityofbath_indoor_tennis_courts_arp.jpg/330px-Universityofbath_indoor_tennis_courts_arp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tennis_court","wikidata":"Q741118"},{"title":"Tennis Court (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Tennis Court\" is a song recorded by New Zealand singer-songwriter Lorde. She co-wrote the song with Joel Little, with production handled by the latter. Universal Music Group (UMG) released the song as the second single from her debut studio album Pure Heroine (2013) in Australia and New Zealand on 7 June 2013. On the same day, the label released an extended play (EP) of the same name containing three additional tracks throughout Europe. It combines alternative pop, art pop, and downtempo music over hip hop beats, minimalist synthesisers, and an electronic pulse. Inspired by Lorde's fresh insights into the music industry, the lyrics address her newfound fame and nostalgia for Auckland."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/10/Lorde_Tennis_Court.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tennis_Court_(song)","wikidata":"Q14664875"},{"title":"Tennis","blocks":[{"text":"Tennis is a racket sport that is played either individually against a single opponent (singles) or between two teams of two players each (doubles). Each player uses a tennis racket strung with a cord to strike a hollow rubber ball covered with felt over or around a net and into the opponent's court. The objective is to manoeuvre the ball in such a way that the opponent is not able to play a valid return. If a player is unable to return the ball successfully, the opponent scores a point."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/2013_Australian_Open_-_Guillaume_Rufin.jpg/330px-2013_Australian_Open_-_Guillaume_Rufin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tennis","wikidata":"Q847"},{"title":"Court","blocks":[{"text":"A court is an institution, often a government entity, with the authority to adjudicate legal disputes between parties and administer justice in civil, criminal, and administrative matters in accordance with the rule of law."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Microcosm_of_London_Plate_058_-_Old_Bailey_edited.jpg/330px-Microcosm_of_London_Plate_058_-_Old_Bailey_edited.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Court","wikidata":"Q41487"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Pet%C3%A4j%C3%A4vesi_-_tennis_court.jpg/500px-Pet%C3%A4j%C3%A4vesi_-_tennis_court.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Pet%C3%A4j%C3%A4vesi_-_tennis_court.jpg/1280px-Pet%C3%A4j%C3%A4vesi_-_tennis_court.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Pet%C3%A4j%C3%A4vesi_-_tennis_court